kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-k9"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-k9"],"id":"long.record-257bm-k9","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.136 (Vanishing of the specified linear-channel determinant)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.136, p. 81, label record:257bm-k9","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $V$ be a vector space over $\\mathbb{Q}$, let $e:V\\to\\mathbb{Q}$ be linear, and let $(\\ell_j)_{j\\in\\iota}$ be a finite family of linear functionals vanishing on $\\ker e$. For any vectors $(v_i)_{i\\in\\iota}$, the matrix $(\\ell_j(v_i))_{i,j\\in\\iota}$ has rank at most one, so every square minor of size at least two vanishes. Indeed, the functionals descend to $V/\\ker e$, which has dimension at most one. This elementary linear-algebra argument applies at every matrix size. It does not cover additional functionals that fail to vanish on $\\ker e$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-k9","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-k9","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-k9%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_relationInvariant_channels_det_eq_zero%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-k9%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_relationInvariant_channels_det_eq_zero%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_relationInvariant_channels_det_eq_zero"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from